{%- import "node/_types.jinja" as types -%}
{#-
  The contract of one table's data layer: create, read, update, delete, and a
  search that filters over several columns and orders by a named column and a
  direction.

  Rendered once per table, per FR-RND-002 and FR-EX-005:

      tpl -d <schema> render node/repository --table <name> > src/<schema>/<name>_repository.js

  The contract is rendered separately from the implementation so that a caller
  can depend on it without depending on how it is served, and so that the
  difference between the two is visible in the example rather than implied.

  **It is a base class, and that is the JavaScript answer to a problem the
  other three examples solved differently.** Go has an `interface`, Rust a
  `trait` and Python a `typing.Protocol`, all of which are satisfied without
  naming them. JavaScript has no structural declaration a `.js` file can carry
  and no `abstract` keyword, so the contract is a class whose every method
  throws, and the implementation extends it. `tsc` then proves the two agree:
  a method whose signature drifted from this one fails with TS2416, and a
  method whose name drifted fails with TS4113, because the implementation tags
  each override with `@override` and `noImplicitOverride` is on. That is the
  same failure the Python example catches with one assignment under
  `TYPE_CHECKING`, and it is the failure this example is most likely to produce
  and the one nothing else would report: `node --check` accepts a repository
  that implements nothing at all.
-#}
{%- if not table.primary_key -%}
{{- fail("node/repository.jinja cannot render " ~ database.name ~ "." ~ table.name ~ ": the table declares no primary key, so read, update and delete have no key to address a row by.") -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set model = types.type_name(table.name) -%}
{%- set module = table.name -%}
{%- set qualified = database.name ~ "." ~ table.name -%}
{%- set auto -%}
{%- for col in table.columns %}{% if col is auto_increment %}<auto>{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- endset -%}
